    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1255">

                <pb facs="1224" n="1058" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg1058"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.5034/30</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Mr.
                            Parker, representing American
                        interests</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-01-06T16:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 6, 1917, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>604. Reported <hi rendition="#italic">de facto</hi> Government recently issued
                    decree giving foreigners holding title to real estate, mining and oil properties
                    and timber lands, until April 15 to resign their treaty rights concerning such
                    properties. Report whether such decree issued.</p>
                <p>Forward another copy of decree issued some months ago requiring foreign
                    purchasers of real estate to resign their rights as nationals.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
